1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Something on this box just took 44% of your VRAM.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Thirty-five workloads on one GPU — LLMs, agents, ROS 2. nvtop tells you it happened, five terminals deep.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
raqib — one pane of glass for everything fighting over your GPU.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Sorts them by what they are. Idle models hold no VRAM — raqib says so instead of guessing. An em dash where the number is unknowable, never a fake 0.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The governor sent one SIGTERM — on its own — and logged exactly why. Nothing else was touched.

6
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Four gates before anything dies. Off by default. The web API can never arm it.

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Open source. Linux. Beta. It watches by default. Killing is your call.
